            <ArticleTitle>Triglyceride-rich lipoproteins and the progression of coronary artery disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>209-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A growing body of evidence from serial coronary angiographic studies indicates that triglyceride-rich lipoproteins are an important factor in the progression of coronary artery disease. Compelling evidence also suggests that triglyceride-rich lipoproteins may be most important in the progression of mild-moderate lesions, the very lesions that are likely to be responsible for clinical coronary events.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
